lesson: 75
title: Two parts and the whole
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes nothing comes or goes: a group is simply made of two parts, like boys and girls in a class.
explain: To find the whole, add the two parts: 12 boys and 9 girls make 12 + 9 = 21 children.
explain: To find one part, take the other part from the whole: 21 children with 12 boys leave 21 - 12 = 9 girls.
vars: a=name x=6..40 p=2..30
need: x - p >= 2
answer: x
exercise: There are {p} boys and {x-p} girls in a class. How many children are in the class?
exercise: {a} has {p} red marbles and {x-p} blue marbles. How many marbles does {a} have?
exercise: A farm has {p} cows and {x-p} sheep. How many animals does the farm have?
exercise: A jar holds {x+p} marbles. {p} of them are red and the rest are blue. How many blue marbles are there?
exercise: There are {x+p} children in the park. {p} are boys. How many are girls?
exercise: {a} has {x+p} flowers. {p} are red and the others are yellow. How many yellow flowers does {a} have?
test: {x-p} girls and {p} boys play in the yard. How many children play in the yard?
test: Of the {x+p} animals on a farm, {p} are cows and the rest are sheep. Find the number of sheep.
test: {a} owns {x+p} pens; only {p} are black and all the others are blue. How many blue pens does {a} own?
test: In a basket lie {p} green apples and {x-p} red ones. How many apples lie in the basket altogether?
exercise: {a} picked {p} apples and {x-p} pears in an orchard in Ohio. How many pieces of fruit did {a} pick altogether?
exercise: How many pupils are in a class in Dublin with {p.words} boys and {x-p} girls?
exercise: A football team in Toronto has {x-p} girls and {p} boys. How many players are on the team in total?
exercise: {a} keeps {p} ducks and {x-p} hens on a farm in Kent. How many birds does {a} keep combined?
exercise: A bag holds {x+p} candies; {p} are lemon and all the rest are cherry. How many cherry candies are in the bag?
exercise: There are {x+p} cars in a car park in Leeds. {p} of them are red. How many cars are not red?
exercise: {a} has {p} stamps from Canada and {x-p} stamps from Australia. How many stamps does {a} have together?
exercise: {x+p} children from a school in Auckland went on a trip. {p} were in Year 3 and the rest were in Year 4. How many children were in Year 4?
test: How many sheep are in a field in Wales if {x-p} are white and {p.words} are black?
test: Out of {x+p} books on a shelf in Sydney, {p} are about animals and the remaining books are stories. How many story books are there?
test: A choir in Boston has {p} boys and {x-p} girls singing in it. Find the total number of singers.
test: {a} counted {x+p} birds at a lake in Ontario: {p} ducks, and all the others geese. How many geese did {a} count?
test: {x-p} oak trees and {p} maple trees grow in a park in Vermont. What is the number of trees in the park?
test: {a}'s jigsaw puzzle has {x+p} pieces, and {p} of them are edge pieces. How many pieces are not edge pieces?
exercise: {p} boys n {x-p} girls in our class, how many of us then
exercise: {a} got {p+1} red marbles — no wait, {p} — and {x-p} blue ones. how many marbles all up
exercise: bag's got {x+p} candies, {p} lemon (gross lol) the rest cherry. how many cherry
exercise: my mate says {p} sheep plus {x-p} cows is {x+p}. nah thats wrong innit, how many animals really
test: farm's got {x-p} hens n {p} ducks, oh and the farmer's like 70 lol. how many birds altogether
