test: {a} says {x-p} girls n {p} boys makes {x+2}?? not right, how many kids altogether
exam: Determine the total enrolment of a class comprising {p} boys and {x-p} girls.
exam: It is given that a collection of marbles consists of {p} red marbles and {x-p} blue marbles, there being no others. Ascertain the cardinality of the collection.
exam: Whereas a whole is composed of two parts, the first of which numbers {x-p} and the second {p}, state the magnitude of the whole.
exam: Compute the aggregate number of persons present, given that {p.words} are seated and {x-p} are standing.
exercise: At the celebration of life for {a}'s grandad there were {p} family members and {x-p} friends. How many people came?
exercise: After the café 'restructured', {a}'s mum works {p} hours a week there and {x-p} hours cleaning offices. How many hours does she work a week?
